###Setting up a proportion

Corresponding sides of similar triangles are proportional, so we can set up and solve a proportion: 

$\dfrac{\blueE{AN}}{OR}=\dfrac{FN}{FR}$

We picked side $\blueE{\overline{AN}}$ because we need to find its length.

We picked side $\overline{OR}$ because it corresponds to side $\blueE{\overline{AN}}$.

Then we picked another pair of corresponding sides where we already knew the measurements.

$\begin{array}{rcl}
&\triangle FAN
\\
{\text{opposite to } \atop \angle F}
&\overbrace{\underbrace{\!\!\!\!\!\left\{ 
\dfrac{\blueE{AN}}{OR}=\dfrac{FN}{FR}
\right\}\!\!\!\!\!}}
&{\text{opposite to } \atop \angle A/\angle O}
\\
&\triangle FOR
\end{array}$

Note that $FR=FO$ since $\triangle FOR$ is an isosceles triangle.
